finding={'kind':'decision_shortcut','description':'The replacement arithmetic_bank makes the correct answer disproportionately the option nearest zero within the recognizable slope_sqrt_radio family. Selecting the unique smallest absolute value, without reading the function or target, succeeds on 4/5 discovery cases and 8/15 fresh unforced cases (53.3% versus 20% blind-choice baseline; held-out binomial tail 0.00424). This is a probabilistic cue, not a universal key. All 15 fresh cases survive delivery, and the actual batch’s sole radio exhibits it. The radius floor of 4 and denominator-weighted distractor pool do not control absolute-magnitude rank when the correct slope is small.','source_refs':['c8b46779-d19f-5cca-987d-5f500a9de334 (q-107360)','67f07fb8-cc06-5cda-9a1f-cc029f68242d (q-107288)','tutorial 743ad997-8732-5c0f-9676-ff1d44f3b513: differentiate inner and outer functions, multiply, then substitute.'],'reproduction':'From evidence_root run /home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/.venv/bin/python -B nearest_zero_regression.py (exit 1). It regenerates slope_sqrt_radio, easy, seeds 764300..764314; no draws are discarded. It also accepts an explicit candidate-records JSON path; delivery-focused/accepted.json reproduces 8/15 and exit 1. Minimal actual-batch witness: seed 3173462203, a=7,b=37,t=-4. For y=sqrt(37+7x), x=-4, choices are 7/6,31/13,-39/14,3,40/13. The smallest absolute value is the correct 7/6. See batch-records.json, delivery-batch/accepted.json and render/question-004.png. A one-item file reports the witness without treating one success alone as statistical proof.','requested_change':'Revise the family-wide arithmetic_bank distractor construction so small correct slopes are not systematically distinguished by absolute magnitude. Control absolute-rank cues as well as signed rank and spacing, or use supported error constructions that avoid this bias. Preserve legitimate coefficients, targets, source families and deterministic replay. Retain the fresh-seed and explicit-candidate regression through delivery; do not fix only this seed or hand-pick a replacement batch. The runner should regenerate its batch after the package repair.'}
result={'verdict':'revise','summary':'The original spacing defect is repaired, but revised slope answer banks favor a nearest-zero shortcut: 8/15 fresh successes versus a 20% baseline, including the actual batch radio. Other seven checks pass; historical affected radios are retired and package files remain unchanged.','source_analysis':source,'checks':checks,'findings':[finding]}
